PART A -- single coprime straddle [Z^q, W, ZW]: charges +q,-1,0.  m0 = q+1.
PREDICTION (THM-415, prime=no collision / composite=collision):
  m0 PRIME  => primitive level saturates alone, M* = m0     (mu=1)
  m0 COMPOSITE => collision needs an extra level, M* > m0    (mu>1)

  q  m0=q+1   factor(m0)   M*   M*/m0  m0 prime?   predict
  1       2       {2: 1}    2    1.00       True      mu=1  MATCH
  2       3       {3: 1}    3    1.00       True      mu=1  MATCH
  3       4       {2: 2}    4    1.00      False      mu>1  <-- BREAKS
  4       5       {5: 1}    5    1.00       True      mu=1  MATCH
  5       6 {2: 1, 3: 1}    6    1.00      False      mu>1  <-- BREAKS
  6       7       {7: 1}    7    1.00       True      mu=1  MATCH
  7       8       {2: 3}    8    1.00      False      mu>1  <-- BREAKS
